{
  "abstract": "For a graph G and integer n, let h_G(n) be the maximum over all n-vertex induced subgraphs of the minimum number of edge deletions needed to make the subgraph bipartite. Erdős, Hajnal, and Szemerédi (1982) constructed a graph G with chromatic number aleph_1 and h_G(n) <= 2 n^(3/2), and Erdős (1981) conjectured that for every ε > 0 there exists a graph G with chromatic number aleph_1 and h_G(n) = O(n^(1+ε)). This package gives an original ZFC machine-checked proof of Erdős's conjecture.",
